.TH FFD 1 "September 2026" "FFD 0.3.13" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
ffd - Fast Fetch Data, a fast command-line downloader

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ffd
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " URL..."
.br
.B ffd proxy
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B ffd update

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ffd
is a fast command-line downloader written in Go.

It supports parallel downloads, multiple HTTP protocols, configurable workers and chunks, retries, custom HTTP headers, and proxy support.

.SH DOWNLOAD

.SS Basic

Download a file:

.PP
.nf
ffd URL
.fi

.PP
Download multiple files:

.PP
.nf
ffd URL1 URL2 URL3
.fi

.SS Options

.TP
.BR -o ", " --output " " NAME
Custom output filename.

.TP
.BR -w ", " --wait " " SECONDS
Wait before downloading.

.TP
.BR -p ", " --path " " PATH
Output directory. The default is the current directory.

.TP
.BR -r ", " --max-retries " " NUMBER
Maximum number of retries. The default is 4.

.TP
.BR -W ", " --max-workers " " NUMBER
Maximum number of concurrent workers. The default is 8.

.TP
.BR -c ", " --max-chunks " " NUMBER
Maximum number of download chunks. The default is 12.

.TP
.B --protocol PROTOCOL
HTTP protocol to use. The default is
.B auto.

.TP
.B --header " " HEADER
Add a custom HTTP header in the format
.B "Header: Value".
This option can be used multiple times.

.TP
.B --set-proxy PROXY
Set a proxy server for downloading.

.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help information.

.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Show the ffd version.

.SS Examples

.TP
.B Download a file
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip
.fi

.TP
.B Download multiple files
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file1.zip https://example.com/file2.zip
.fi

.TP
.B Custom filename
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip -o my-file.zip
.fi

.TP
.B Custom download directory
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip -p ~/Downloads
.fi

.TP
.B More workers and chunks
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip -W 16 -c 20
.fi

.TP
.B Force HTTP/2
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip --protocol http2
.fi

.TP
.B Wait before downloading
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip -w 10
.fi

.TP
.B Increase retries
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip -r 10
.fi

.TP
.B Add a custom HTTP header
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip --header "User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0"
.fi

.TP
.B Add multiple HTTP headers
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip \\
  --header "User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0" \\
  --header "Authorization: Bearer TOKEN"
.fi

.TP
.B Set a proxy for downloading
.PP
.nf
ffd https://example.com/file.zip --set-proxy http://127.0.0.1:8000
.fi

.SH PROXY

The
.B proxy
command starts the ffd forward proxy.

.SS Usage

Start the proxy with the default configuration:

.PP
.nf
ffd proxy
.fi

.PP
By default, the proxy listens on:

.PP
.nf
127.0.0.1:8000
.fi

.SS Options

.TP
.B --port PORT
Set the local proxy listening port.

.TP
.B --set-proxy PROXY
Set an upstream proxy server for the ffd proxy.

.PP
For example:

.PP
.nf
ffd proxy --port 9000
.fi

.PP
Set an upstream proxy:

.PP
.nf
ffd proxy --set-proxy http://127.0.0.1:9000
.fi

.SH UPDATE

The
.B update
command updates ffd to the latest version.

.PP
.nf
ffd update
.fi

